t"]}}`, built from its cause's fixed strings — sent on the session socket as `ok v3 refused <json>` and written to the `escher-session` client's stdout with status 1, and a `SessionError` is written likewise as `{"error":{"kind","message"}}` — since 2026-10-12-self-description `{"error":{"kind","message","remedy"}}` — `kind` one fixed kebab-case word per variant; since that chunk each error's kind, meaning and remedy are one row of the crate-private table `SESSION_ERRORS: [ErrorSpec; 15]` — `RecordDirNotPrivate` (`record-dir-not-private`) and `RecordingFailed` (`recording-failed`) its rows since 2026-10-19-session-recording, each exit `3`, so `help`'s `session_errors` serves 15 — which `kind()`, the new public `remedy()` and `Display` read (`Display` the row's meaning, the `Io` and `NotSettled` arms adding their detail as before), two rows sharing a remedy, each later row naming the earlier (`dead` · `no-session`, `answer-too-large` · `not-settled`), and `StateDirTooLong`'s message states its bound as a figure, 94 bytes as given on Linux and 90 elsewhere — each measured, the 90 on the macOS CI leg since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep (CI#38642493451) —, holding no path — every text a fixed string of the table, served by `help` and carried on stdout and in MCP results as the program's own fixed text inside the ratified carriers, ratified by the founder (2026-10-12, «Внутри, с правилом», by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer) (packages/escher-driver/src/error.rs:79-177; packages/escher-driver/src/error.rs:61-69 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-self-description/report.md); the node keys' help since that chunk also states the boolean model's two limits; since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface each is also an MCP tool result, `{content:[{type:"text",text}], isError: true}`, the same JSON as its text — a refused `screenshot` included, one text block — (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp/result.rs:29-104), and an MCP protocol error is a fixed code and a fixed message — `parse error` · `invalid request` · `method not found` · `invalid params` · `unknown tool` — with no `data` (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp/framing.rs:100-129), the admitted request `id` the one client-sent value written back — measured: no reply holds the refused id, the tool name or the filler (`mcp_server`); neither holds anything a call supplied (until then a refusal was held in process only); and since 2026-10-07-driver-command-spans exactly one thing of a refusal reaches a log: its cause's fixed name, recorded as the `cause` field of the call's `escher_driver` span at one site for every refusal `Session::run` returns, whichever of `validate` and the executor returned it; no `Fault`, meaning, remedy or `Display` text is fielded — a `malformed` call's line reads `cause="malformed"` and nothing of the rule it broke — and a cause name holds nothing a call supplied (packages/escher-driver/src/refusal.rs:131-142; packages/escher-driver/src/refusal.rs:160-163; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:257-262) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-command-and-refusal-schema/report.md, the two reworded texts at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md, the logged cause name at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md
